   342	## 6. Sources and snapshots
   343	
   344	### 6.1 Canonical source identity
   345	
   346	Network git sources use a canonical identity. Local paths and `file:` URLs have
   347	no network identity. Protocol 1.0 network URLs:
   348	
   349	- use `ssh`, `git`, `http`, or `https`, or SCP form `[user@]host:path`;
   350	- have an ASCII host matching `[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9.-]*`;
   351	- contain no explicit port, password, query, fragment, percent escape, or
   352	  backslash;
   353	- contain a non-empty portable repository path with no whitespace, `%`, `?`,
   354	  or `#` character;
   355	- produce a canonical `host/path` identity of at most 4096 Unicode scalar
   356	  values.
   357	
   358	Canonicalization lowercases the host, removes user and transport, trims outer
   359	path slashes, and removes one case-sensitive trailing `.git`. Repository path
   360	case is preserved. The result is `host/path`. Invalid network forms MUST be
   361	rejected, not treated as local.
   362	
   363	Allowlist matching is segment-aware: identity `h/a/b` matches prefix `h/a` but
   364	not `h/a-evil`. An empty allowlist permits all network identities. Local
   365	sources bypass the network allowlist.
