   367	### 6.2 Git safety and references
   368	
   369	Git execution MUST restrict protocols to `file`, `git`, `http`, `https`, and
   370	`ssh`; refuse empty or dash-prefixed operands; and place untrusted operands
   371	after `--` where supported. Submodules are unsupported. Archive extraction
   372	MUST reject symbolic links, hard links, path escapes, duplicate platform paths,
   373	and entries exceeding implementation limits documented by the manager.
   374	
   375	Tags resolve `refs/tags/<value>^{commit}`. Revisions resolve
   376	`<value>^{commit}`. Branches prefer `refs/remotes/origin/<value>` and then a
   377	local head. A resolved commit is the full lowercase hexadecimal object id
   378	returned by git. Snapshots are immutable regular-file trees produced from that
   379	commit.
