   381	## 7. Closure resolution
   382	
   383	Direct declarations enter as `full` requirements from synthetic consumer
   384	`<project>`. Processing a provider adds its skill requirements.
   385	
   386	Within one closure, one skill name MUST resolve to exactly one commit and one
   387	canonical source identity. Different identities or commits fail with every
   388	relevant requirement chain. Different refs resolving to one commit unify.
   389	Cycles fail and name the cycle.
   390	
   391	Activation is edge-based. Context is active when any incoming edge is `full`
   392	or `context`. All commands are active when any edge is `full`; otherwise the
   393	active set is the union of runtime edges, narrowed where requested.
   394	
   395	Provider order is deterministic Kahn topological order: among currently ready
   396	providers select the lexicographically smallest skill name by Unicode scalar
   397	value. The synthetic project is not emitted. Diagnostic requirement chains use
   398	the lexicographically smallest complete chain when multiple chains are equal
   399	in length.
